Subject: [PATCH 10683/11171] Fourth quarantine confirms the prediction and
 widens it: a quoted path is enough

The 20:37Z entry predicted the next per-family CPU artifact in this lineage would be
flagged. It was. But exp6857 also shows the "lineage" framing was too narrow, so the
entry now corrects itself rather than leaving that to be re-derived.

exp6857 is a read-only artifact DISCOVERY task, substrate
read_only_terminal_live_artifact_discovery, 1.048597s. No per-family analysis. It was
flagged because a model path it discovered while reading other artifacts contains the
marker: .../models--unsloth--Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF/snapshots/...

The accurate statement is that the scan cannot distinguish an artifact that RAN a
model from one that TALKS ABOUT models, including one that merely quotes a filesystem
path. Any router, inventory, or discovery task over a model-bearing corpus trips it.
Per-family analysis is one instance of that class, not the class.

New cost class, worse than the previous one. Until now the damage was exclusion from
aggregation. This time a dependent task was refused outright: exp6858's gate required
exp6857 terminal-clean, that gate failed, and exp6858 was GATE_BLOCKed with
blocked_gate_check_failed.

exp6858 is the Supervisor counterfactual credit audit. So the false quarantine is now
blocking the supervisor-credit program that exp6844 and exp6845 already reported as
evidence-starved. The defect no longer only mislabels honest work; it prevents the
work that would answer the open question.

Confirmed count 4: exp6840, exp6853, exp6856, exp6857. Blocked downstream: 1.

